      "summaryMarkdown": "This is a full review at revision 8. A reattestation was not possible because the specification amendment dropped the stored review. The REPO-1 to REPO-4 texts are unchanged, so the earlier inspection holds, and I inspected the repair batch on top of it.\n\n- **REPO-1:** the package fields, the 1.99.0 toolchain and the thin `main.rs` are as required. `--version` prints `rayx 1.0.0`, `--help` lists exactly the ten commands, unknown commands and flags exit 2 with usage, and every command is a stub that exits 1. `rayx app` passes everything after the nsh command raw, `--` included.\n- **REPO-2:** `dependency_sources` is a verbatim port. `library_guard` has a failing fixture per rule and a stale-allowlist case. Test-only child modules now resolve correctly (S1-F5), and the `env!` match covers bracket, brace and multi-line calls.\n- **REPO-3:** CI runs on pull requests and on pushes to `main` in `rayx-ui/RayX.CLI` only, with fmt, clippy and test on the three OS runners. `release.yml` is unchanged from dist 0.33.0, and the YAML check passes. `d-release` now declares that it supersedes the old pull-request-only invariant (S1-F3). The owner's explicit confirmation is still pending through the coordinator.\n- **REPO-4:** every configuration value is correct. `release_policy.rs` now asserts the policy comment, the changelog header and each `docs/releasing.md` section the criterion lists (S1-F1). `d-release` and OWN-4 match the documented first release with no pull request (S1-F4).\n\nChecks reran at this snapshot and were reused: 41, 21 and the YAML check. Cosmetic only: line 4 of `release-plz.yml` is 138 characters. The port commit must still name `d006250`.",
